---
const title = "Privacy Notice | Test Before You Build";
const description =
  "How Test Before You Build handles the personal information submitted through this website.";
const canonical = "https://testbeforeyoubuild.com/privacy/";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <a href="/">← Test Before You Build</a>
    </header>
    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>How we handle your information</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This notice explains how Test Before You Build and Kari Jääskeläinen
        handle information submitted through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form asks for your name, email address, and a description of
        the idea you want to discuss. You may also choose to provide information
        about the intended customer and the problem the idea is designed to solve.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use the information to respond to your enquiry, assess whether the
        validation service may be relevant, and discuss possible next steps. We do
        not use information submitted through the form to train AI models.
      </p>

      <h2>How the form is delivered</h2>
      <p>
        The form is processed by Formspree, which acts as a service provider for
        delivering your message. Avoid including confidential technical details,
        trade secrets, health information, or other sensitive personal data in
        your first message.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries only for as long as they are needed to respond, manage a
        possible customer relationship, and meet applicable legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask what personal information we hold about you or request its
        correction or deletion when applicable. You can make that request by using
        the contact form on the homepage and stating that your message concerns
        privacy.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: 11 September 2026</p>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <a href="/">Return to the homepage</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    color: #0d1930;
    background: #f5f8fc;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; }
  header, main, footer { width: min(760px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; }
  header { padding: 30px 0; }
  main { margin-top: 28px; padding: 48px; border: 1px solid #d8e0ec; border-radius: 24px; background: #fff; }
  footer { padding: 30px 0 50px; }
  a { color: #155eef; font-weight: 750; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 12px; color: #155eef; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.4rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  h2 { margin: 36px 0 8px; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  p { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #536781; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.18rem; color: #405573; }
  .updated { margin-top: 40px; font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { main { padding: 30px 24px; } }
</style>
